WEBVTT

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:17.490
Thirteen years had passed since 
the end of the Pacific War.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.430
Japan had overcome the postwar disarray

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.070
and was about to enter a 
period of rapid growth.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.440
<b>Protect Life</b>

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.420
<b>Nagashima joins the Giants</b>

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:33.050
But in the underworld beneath 
that sheen, where evil spirits lurk,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:36.070
a legend was about to be born.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.860
<b>The world's tallest broadcasting tower</b>

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.580
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.580
<b>The Genius Who Descended 
Into the Darkness</b>

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.620
The legend of the man who would

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.490
soon be called man from 
the godly realm and

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.520
who would rule the underworld.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.960
<i>Typhoon number 21 will...</i>

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.470
<i>What I wanted...</i>

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.520
<i>was change.</i>

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:08.500
<i>The kind of change that would 
turn everything around.</i>

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.710
<i>To the point of rebirth.</i>

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.820
Nangou-san, that's it. Ron.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.820
Ron - Winning a hand with an opponent's discard.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.510
Mangan - A hand worth 8,000 points (12,000 for the dealer.)

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.510
Mangan.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.190
<b>Nangou</b>

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.430
<i>My debts from the stock market, 
my losses from gambling...</i>

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.190
<i>Everything I touched, I messed up.</i>

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.160
<i>And tonight...</i>

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.340
<i>The game of Mahjong I am 
playing to erase my debt,</i>

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.350
<i>I am losing, as well.</i>

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.910
<i>When this is over, I'll have 
to repay a huge debt.</i>

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.650
<i>The life insurance I signed 
up for last month...</i>

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:51.380
<i>the beneficiary is the mistress 
of this man, Ryuuzaki.</i>

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.380
<b>Ryuuzaki</b>

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.890
<b>- Next Turn -</b>

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.230
<i>They've cornered me.</i>

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.390
<i>I can't deal into his hand any more.</i>

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.390
<i>This one should be safe!</i>

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:06.630
Ron!

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.030
<i>Calm down!</i>

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.480
<i>I've got do something. Anything!</i>

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.890
<b>- South Hand 3 -</b>

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.500
<i>My starting tiles are so bad, 
they make me want to cry.</i>

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.130
<i>If I finish last in this East-South 
match, I'm done for.</i>

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.370
<i>Please!</i>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.720
<i>Nothing's happening!</i>

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.940
<i>Please, someone change this! 
I don't care who does it.</i>

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.920
<i>This stagnant air... 
Someone, please, mix up the flow!</i>

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.320
<i>I don't care who!</i>

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.050
<i>Even if it's the devil!</i>

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.490
Who's there?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.730
Who the hell are you?!

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.330
Find somewhere else to hide from the rain!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.250
This isn't a place for kids!

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.180
Go home already.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.150
Wait! I invited that kid.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:43.390
I told him to come check on me if 
he didn't hear from me by midnight.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.260
<i>Of course, that was a lie.</i>

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.820
<i>I didn't know that kid.</i>

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.060
<i>All I wanted was a break.</i>

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.200
<i>A chance to turn the tide.</i>

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.730
<i>Look at them.</i>

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.600
<i>They all look deflated.</i>

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.030
<i>It's clear that the heat 
of the game is fading.</i>

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:12.060
<i>The tide could still turn...</i>

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:17.560
<i>I have to somehow pull through and turn 
it around in the next East-South match.</i>

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:19.620
<i>Hang in there!</i>

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.040
<i>Don't give up!</i>

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:26.800
<b>- South Hand 4 -</b>

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.920
And on the eighth turn of South Hand 4,

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.670
an opportunity finally arises.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:35.520
<i>This is it!</i>

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.610
<i>I can discard the 5 of circles 
and wait for a 1 or 4.</i>

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.690
<i>If I get the best case, 1 of circles,</i>

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.790
Sanshoku - Same sequence (triplets) of all 3 suits. 
Chanta - Hand with a terminal (1 or 9) or honor tile in each set. 
Haneman - 1.5x mangan.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.790
<i>the red dragon, sanshoku, and chanta 
will give me a haneman with one dora.</i>

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.870
<i>I could even take over the lead.</i>

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.330
<i>The problem is the riichi across from me.</i>

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.330
Riichi - The player declares he is one tile away from winning and
wagers 1,000 points for the chance to further increase his score.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:00.300
<i>I really want to discard the 5 of circles, 
but it's pretty dangerous.</i>

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.310
<i>I can't push my luck here.</i>

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.380
<i>It'll end up a cheap, red dragon only hand...</i>

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.980
<i>but the 2 of circles is already a safe tile.</i>

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.810
<i>If I deal into his hand, 
everything is over.</i>

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.850
You'd survive if you only died.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.630
Do you know how to play Mahjong, kid?

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.790
No, not at all.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.760
But your spirit had died just now.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.110
Your back shows you don't 
have the strength to win.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.320
You're just trying to survive.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.530
That's the final thought pattern of gamblers

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.410
who have been on a losing streak.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.890
You're just scared.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:06:59.950
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.980
<i>That kid's right.</i>

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:06.230
<i>How could I discard the 
2 of circles with this hand?!</i>

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.990
<i>I don't know what I was thinking.</i>

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.750
<i>I'm gambling right now.</i>

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.580
<i>How can I win if I don't take any chances?</i>

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.820
<i>If I'm going to die anyway,</i>

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.210
<i>I might as well go out hitting hard!</i>

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.120
<i>It worked.</i>

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:29.060
At that moment,

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.830
the largely ignored player to his 
right was actually in tenpai.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.830
Tenpai - One tile away from winning.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.220
He was waiting for a green 
dragon or a 2 of circles.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:40.070
Had Nangou "fled" with the 2 of circles, 
he would have dealt into his hand.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.470
A trick of fate.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.940
After that, the player to his 
right draws a 1 of circles.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.030
He could have kept it and 
dealt the safe 2 of circles,

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.950
but he keeps going, aiming for a san ankou.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.950
San ankou - Three concealed triplets.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.190
Ron!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.090
From that moment,

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:05.510
the pendulum of the game started 
to slowly swing in Nangou's favor.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.580
<i>I took the lead.</i>

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.350
<i>I survived.</i>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.150
Kid, how old are you?

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.160
Thirteen.

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:36.260
You don't look it.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:36.890
What's your name?

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:38.640
Akagi.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.400
Akagi Shigeru.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.290
What exactly did you do?

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.360
You're wandering around 
on a stormy night like this,

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.260
waltzing into a Mahjong parlor 
you know nothing about.

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:53.710
The only obvious thing is that 
you're not a normal student.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.500
And that sand on your shirt...

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.530
Been swimming in the 
ocean this late at night?

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.620
I know.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.420
You don't want to talk about it.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.590
You probably walked the line

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.900
between life and death 
before you came here.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:18.400
I can sense it because I am 
treading that line right now.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:23.750
I mean, if I don't win tonight, 
I'm gonna be killed.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:29.860
Please, will you play the next 
East-South match in my place?

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:35.680
I can feel that you have 
what it takes to compete...

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.660
Zeal, luck, and heart.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.330
You can make it across that line.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.460
This is the beginning of 
the legend Akagi Shigeru,

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:01.240
who will soon rock the foundation 
of the underground Mahjong world.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:04.380
His first time playing Mahjong.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:09.210
Just five minutes before 
the game started,

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.220
he was only taught the most 
basic rules of Mahjong.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.990
He doesn't know any yaku.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.990
Yaku - Winning hand compositions.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.490
He was less than a beginner.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:22.460
As he plays, Akagi will grasp 
Mahjong little by little.

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.160
That a hand in Mahjong

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.830
is made up of four melds of 
three tiles, plus one pair.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:28.470
<b>Juntsu (Sequence)           Koutsu (Triplet)</b>

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:32.150
That it is a game where players 
compete on the speed, composition,

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.810
<b>1 Han                                 (Pinfu)</b>

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.440
<b>2 Han                    (Sanshoku Doujun)</b>

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.930
and points attributed to their hands.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:34.470
<b>3 Han                             (Hon'iisou)</b>

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.370
That it is usually best to avoid calling

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.850
<b>Menzen</b>

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.960
other players' tiles to build your hand.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:38.710
<b>Pon
Chi</b>

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.000
That the white, green, and red dragons

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.450
<b>Riichi Wager                         1,000 points</b>

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.120
are useful tiles because a triplet 
of either of them is worth 1 han.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.130
Tsumo.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.130
Tsumo - Declaring a winning hand on your draw.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:52.360
That there is a special yaku called 
chiitoitsu that consists of seven pairs.

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:57.770
By the end of the East round, 
Akagi has lost 7,200 points.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:00.600
He hasn't dealt into anybody's hand, 
nor has he won himself.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.440
Quite an ordinary outcome.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.160
His talent, that will eventually earn him

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.500
the title of genius, is not yet apparent.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:11.620
<b>- South Hand 2 -</b>

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:11.220
In South Hand 2, something happens.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.820
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.700
<i>The seed for a daisangen.</i>

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:17.550
Daisangen - A yakuman hand with triplets 
of all 3 dragons (yakuman - 4x mangan)

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.550
<i>He has the three pairs for it!</i>

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:25.010
<i>He can go for a daisangen with this hand.</i>

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.200
<i>If he pulls this off...</i>

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.110
The first red dragon.

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.510
But Akagi lets it pass.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.510
Akagi ignores the following 
white and green dragons, as well.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:42.430
He doesn't make his move.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.380
He stays quiet.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.510
Then comes the second...

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.020
<i>Why?!</i>

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.760
<i>Now he can't do any better than a chiitoitsu!</i>

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:59.100
<i>It's over. He needed to call those tiles.</i>

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:03.480
<i>Even if you didn't know 
what a daisangen was,</i>

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.770
<i>having three of each honor tile
gives you a beastly hand!</i>

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:10.310
<i>That much should be obvious!</i>

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:15.140
<i>I was crazy to put everything 
into this kid's hands.</i>

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:18.550
<i>I'll have to play again myself starting 
from the next East-South match.</i>

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:25.790
Someone's coming up the stairs.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.880
Who's coming here so late at night?

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:35.920
Yes, sir.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:41.310
Who is it?

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:45.080
Excuse me for disturbing you 
so late. It's the police.

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:48.980
There was a bit of an 
incident earlier this evening.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.320
It was a gang rivalry incident.

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.620
I think they call it a game of chicken?

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:02.830
Two cars head straight for 
a cliff at full speed.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.760
It's a game of reckless disregard for life

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:09.050
where the person who brakes first loses.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.290
Well, while they were doing that,

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.990
they didn't brake in time,

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:18.280
so both cars ended up in the ocean.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:21.700
One of the kids was brought to the 
hospital with serious injuries,

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.680
but apparently the other one

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.520
swam to shore by himself 
and fled the scene.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:31.650
We received a report that he 
came to this neighborhood.

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:34.530
That's why we came here 
to ask some questions.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:37.330
A chicken game survivor.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.520
No wonder I thought he was gutsy.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:41.870
What should we do?

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:43.630
Send them away.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.610
Having the cops here will be 
inconvenient for us, as well.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:47.380
Yes, sir.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.000
Nangou-san.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.610
Shall we make a deal?

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:57.130
The cops came here 
because they had a lead,

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:58.990
so they probably won't leave.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.790
They'll push their way 
in here any minute now.

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:05.010
When that happens, all I need 
is for our stories to match,

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.720
and for you to vouch for 
my alibi and identity.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:10.690
<i>This damn kid. He's out of his mind.</i>

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:12.770
<i>Why should I do all that for him?</i>

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.700
Gimme a break.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.560
You can't make a deal if you 
don't have something to offer!

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:24.480
But I have something.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.410
Suu ankou - Four concealed triplets, a double 
yakuman when waiting for a single tile.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.410
<i>Suu ankou, daisangen, 
waiting for a single west wind!</i>

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:31.750
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.150
<i>Just a moment ago, his hand was...</i>

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:37.830
<i>He swapped them!</i>

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.890
<i>He took them from the discard pile</i>

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.520
<i>while everybody's attention 
was on the door earlier!</i>

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.270
<i>The one who should be most worried</i>

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.270
<i>about the police approaching</i>

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:47.610
<i>pulled off something like this...</i>

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.940
<i>This kid's got nerves like no other.</i>

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:53.940
<i>He's insane.</i>

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:55.990
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.460
<i>This brat!</i>

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:12.540
<i>But if he discards the red dragon, 
my chance of winning is gone.</i>

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.520
<i>Oh, all right, kid.</i>

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:20.670
<i>I don't have the luxury of choice right now.</i>

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.560
<i>Do what you want.</i>

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:31.180
You didn't make this easy on us, did you?

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:32.770
U-Uh...

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:40.620
There he is.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.850
The kid we're looking for, right here.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.520
Hey, kid.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:49.300
You heard what we said, right?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.260
<i>Damn, this is annoying.</i>

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:54.540
You're the survivor, aren't you?

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.110
Detective,

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:58.560
you're mistaking him for someone else.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.440
He's my older brother's kid.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:03.040
I had to take him in for a while.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:06.180
He's been here in this Mahjong 
parlor since six last night.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:10.680
With us. Right, Ryuuzaki-san?

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:14.180
Ah, yeah, huh?

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:19.760
<i>Ryuuzaki doesn't want the 
cops snooping around, either.</i>

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.690
<i>He'll have no choice but to help us.</i>

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.960
But we had some eye witnesses.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:30.470
And there are footprints on the stairs.

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:34.260
Soaking wet footprints made 
by that kid over there.

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:39.010
Detective, I made those when my uncle

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.180
sent me to go buy cigarettes.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.280
In the middle of the night?

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.580
Yeah, I told him I couldn't go at his hour,

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.690
but he wouldn't take no for an answer.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.580
He was also pretty irritated 
because he'd been losing a lot.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.420
Right?

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:57.340
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:58.930
And, Detective,

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.450
would someone who did 
something like that

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.430
be relaxing and playing Mahjong?

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:10.440
Even if he was, why should 
the people here cover for him?

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.600
There's nothing for them 
to gain from that.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:15.450
I see.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:18.720
So, shall we begin?

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:20.590
Your turn.

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:21.690
Oh, yeah.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:22.870
<i>He's good.</i>

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:27.920
<i>He made them resume the game while 
their focus is still on the cops.</i>

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.260
<i>He's swiped an enormous amount 
of tiles from the discard pile.</i>

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:35.290
<i>If you paid even a little bit 
of attention, you'd notice.</i>

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:40.050
<i>That's why now's his chance, before they 
all return their attention to the game.</i>

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:44.300
<i>They're not thinking right now. 
It's a state of confusion.</i>

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:46.820
<i>Right now, they might just discard it!</i>

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.520
Ron.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.010
Akagi's plot was complemented with luck.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.260
Suu ankou, daisangen.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.050
Wha—

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.690
What is this?!

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.630
You bastard!

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.010
You think you can screw with us?!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:07.900
Stop it.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.230
But, Bro!

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.280
<i>He had factored this in, too?!</i>

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.550
<i>This kid's a monster.</i>

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:26.420
<i>This isn't something a middle 
schooler could think up.</i>

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.960
<i>Everybody knows that he cheated.</i>

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.560
<i>Normally the yakuza would 
not let this slide.</i>

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.780
<i>They'd use force if necessary.</i>

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:40.520
<i>To prevent that option, he lured 
the cops here to be witnesses.</i>

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.470
Bro, are you really okay with this?!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.100
What's okay doesn't matter.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.290
The ones who were cheated are the fools.

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:50.170
But, kid,

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:54.310
make sure this is the last time.

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:56.940
If you do it again and get caught,

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.680
in our world, it'll cost you your fingers.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.880
Cry all you want, but we won't let it slide.

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:04.190
We've never let anyone off 
the hook, not even once!

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:07.260
Messing with the yakuza will net you

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:09.280
the harshest punishment in the world.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.910
Nothing will be taken into consideration.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:15.430
<b>Lounge</b>

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:18.940
That kid's creepy, huh?

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:22.690
Since he got here, 
they've won twice in a row.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.440
Should we contact Yagi-san?

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:31.680
Yagi? You mean our rep player, Yagi Keiji?

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:32.680
Y-Yes...

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.780
Are you delirious?!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.890
You want to ask for backup when 
we're playing this amateur child?

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:45.230
Do you have no honor?!

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:51.990
All he did was cheat his way to a yakuman.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.040
I won't let him do that again!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:59.500
It's a miracle that amateur 
hasn't dealt into any hand yet.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:03.020
That kind of coincidence 
is not going to last!

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:05.350
His luck has run out!

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:12.560
<b>- East Hand 1 -</b>

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.240
Inspector, are you going to stay here?

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:19.580
Yeah, it's still raining buckets, 
so I'm going to take it easy a bit longer.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:22.570
Then, I'll be going.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:23.480
Sure.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:29.440
You don't mind, right, Nangou-san?

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.810
N-Not at all.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:38.280
<i>Don't underestimate me, kid.</i>

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:44.150
<i>No matter how well you craft your 
excuses, I know you are the one.</i>

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:50.820
<i>The atmosphere in here tells me that, 
louder than any words could.</i>

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:56.020
<i>I'm going to find out the truth about you!</i>

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.500
The genius who descended into 
the darkness, Akagi Shigeru.

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:04.560
Beyond his eyes lies an infinite darkness.

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:08.290
This is the beginning of the legend.

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:20.010
Next time: "The Awakening of Talent."

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Awakening of Talent</b>
